From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:37:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: t7: scale the CPU up to 2.208 GHz

Clock the CPUs from the T7 CPU clock controller instead of the SCMI
clocks, which stop at 1.704 GHz. Use binned OPP tables with the vendor
voltages, up to 2.208 GHz on the A73 and 2.016 GHz on the A53 cluster.

On Khadas VIM4, give the CPU regulators a ramp delay: the filtered PWM
output needs time to reach a new voltage.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 .../amlogic/amlogic-t7-a311d2-khadas-vim4.dts |  4 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-t7.dtsi   | 82 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-t7-a311d2-khadas-vim4.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-t7-a311d2-khadas-vim4.dts
index dc7c712cc48f..d7dc6f614184 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-t7-a311d2-khadas-vim4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-t7-a311d2-khadas-vim4.dts
@@ -270,6 +270,8 @@ vddcpua: regulator-vddcpu-a {
 		regulator-name = "VDDCPU_A";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <689000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1049000>;
+		/* the filtered PWM output needs time to settle */
+		regulator-ramp-delay = <150>;
 		pwms = <&pwm_ao_cd 1 1500 0>;
 		voltage-table = <1049000 0>,
 				<1039000 3>,
@@ -317,6 +319,8 @@ vddcpub: regulator-vddcpu-b {
 		regulator-name = "VDDCPU_B";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <689000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1049000>;
+		/* the filtered PWM output needs time to settle */
+		regulator-ramp-delay = <150>;
 		pwms = <&pwm_ao_ab 1 1500 0>;
 		voltage-table = <1049000 0>,
 				<1039000 3>,
